WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.701
-Doesn't it feel good?
-Yeah, this chair feels great.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.300
-It does.
And we get to talk about --

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.767
-There's just
no chair like this.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.868
-Oh, I'm so happy.
-And I get to talk about myself.

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:10.033
-Welcome home!
-Come on!

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.234
-Welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:12.734
-We got to talk
about the projects

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:13.968
that you've worked so hard on.

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:17.267
-I'm so happy to do that.
Are you okay with that?

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.200
-Oh, yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.601
-Then Let's do it.
-Let's do it.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:21.667
Before --
-Okay, okay.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:22.701
What are we gonna do?

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:23.701
-Before we get into it,
I just --

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:24.868
-Oh, this is important.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:26.501
-I have to talk about --
you have a new person

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:27.634
in your life -- a new --

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.334
-Well, person.
-A person in your life.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.801
-I have a Muppet in my life.
-You have a Muppet in your life.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.934
And I want to know all about...
[ Audience "Awws!" ]

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:36.200
-Yes.
-He is very cute.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.234
-He's so cute, and I'm sorry
to have kept him from you,

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:40.801
but his name is Six-Thirty,
and I thought maybe

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:43.334
I was breaking the strike
if I talked about him.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.100
I did not pick his name.
He picked it.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.634
I just don't have the heart
to tell him that

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:48.534
it's just totally absurd
and inappropriate.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.267
-Six-Thirty is his name.
-Yes.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.234
-How did he pick his name?

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:57.167
-Well, he's a rescue and he was
very shy when I first got him.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.701
We were trying all kinds
of different names.

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:01.367
My friends were throwing out,
like, everything under the sun.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.701
And my best friend,

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.868
who is the food consultant
on "Lessons in Chemistry,"

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:06.434
she saw him and was like,
"Oh, my gosh!

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:07.968
He's Six-Thirty."

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:09.801
And he looked up, and I was
like, "Well, that's strange.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:14.367
No." And then we said it again,
and I still didn't believe it.

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:16.934
And he just only
responded to "Six-Thirty."

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.534
I tried everything.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:20.701
I had four days
where I was calling him Dog.

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:22.133
I was calling him --
I don't know --

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:23.901
Jeremy, Jimmy, David.

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.267
-You tried Jimmy, yeah.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:27.601
-I'd be opening the pantry
and be like, "Are you flour?

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:30.067
Are you salt?
Are you black pepper?"

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:31.868
I don't know.
-Six-Thirty, he turns around.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.400
-Mm-hmm.
-That's his name. He chose it.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.334
-He chose it, so please just
respect him when you see him.

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:39.701
His vet thinks it's ridiculous,
His vet is confused.

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:41.934
Yes, the receptionist would go,
"You're Six-Thirty's here."

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.834
And he's like, "It's 2:00.
I don't know what that means."

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.968
-It's very confusing.
-Yeah, it's confusing.

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:47.400
-Can we talk about
"Lessons in Chemistry"?

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.267
-I'd love to.
-By the way, this is great.

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you so much.

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:52.701
-Congratulations on this.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:56.300
You're you're phenomenal in it,
but you also produced it.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.467
How did you get involved
with this?

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:00.300
-It was brought to me and it
was actually brought to me

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.400
about two years
before the book even came out.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.767
-It's a great book.
-Yeah, it's a fabulous book.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.901
And it took about that long
to get it off the ground.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:08.834
But, yeah, they asked me
to be a producer,

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:09.934
which has just been amazing,

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.934
because it helps me
with somebody --

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.767
Like, when I'm playing
someone like Elizabeth,

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.033
who's just such
a rich character,

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:17.734
it's nice to help
build her world

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:18.901
and be there
from the beginning.

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:21.601
And to be totally honest,
I've done this --

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:22.968
I've been acting
since I was like 7

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.467
and I've never really known
what a producer does.

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.501
I'm like, "Yeah, whatever."
Actually, they do a lot.

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:27.767
-Really, yeah. You learned?

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:29.234
-Let me tell you.
-You learned.

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:32.400
-Yeah, I learned that it's hard.
But it was just incredible.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.334
We had the most incredible
cast and crew,

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:36.801
and I'm just happy
to finally say like,

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.901
"Hi, and I love you to everybody
who did 'Lessons in Chemistry.'"

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:40.501
-Yeah.
-You did such a great job.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.601
I'm so proud of what we did.

00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:45.400
-It's phenomenal. Please watch.
-Hi, Bonnie! Hi, Lee!

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.200
-Yes, hi, everyone.
Please watch.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.467
It's actually --
It's phenomenal.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.200
It's well-done,
well-shot, everything.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.701
The sets, the costume,
the wardrobe, the acting.

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:55.234
Obviously, it's all good.
And I love the book, as well.

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:56.634
So congrats on that.
-Thank you.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:03:00.334
-And then we can talk about
your giant movie, "The Marvels."

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:02.667
"The Marvels"
is in theaters today.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:03.767
-Yeah, right now.

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:05.100
-This weekend, go see
"The Marvels."

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.467
You're back.
-Yes, please do.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:08.300
I'd appreciate if you did.
-You back as Captain Marvel.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.734
-I'm back, yeah, and I brought
some friends this time.

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:11.934
-Yeah, you did.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:14.434
You know, gosh,
you've been on our show

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:16.434
even before you were cast
as Captain Marvel,

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:17.501
because I remember talking,

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.067
but I
remember how exciting it was,

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:20.767
like, "Oh, my gosh,
you're Captain Marvel.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.267
This is massive."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:24.767
-And then we just had Iman on
the show, who plays Ms. Marvel.

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:25.934
-Oh, my heart.

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:29.501
-She's so cool
and just the coolest kid.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.734
I mean, she really is a kid.

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:33.567
And she said that you were
the first person

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:38.133
from the Marvel Universe to
call her and congratulate her.

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.667
-Yeah, I was, I was.

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.934
Yeah, I just think being
a superhero is, like,

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:44.100
a weird, specific job.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.167
It's just like,
who else is going to be like,

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:47.734
"And make sure you have
extra zippers

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:49.100
so you can go
to the bathroom"?

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.300
You know, it's just, like,
very strange things.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.167
And I felt really lucky,
because the first time

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.934
I played Captain Marvel
was on "Avengers,"

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.767
and so I had Scarlett Johansson

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.133
was the first person
who welcomed me,

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.367
and I got to be there
with all of them.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.234
-She called you first?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:05.334
And, so, to have them
not just welcome me in,

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:06.767
but to also just be like,
"You've got this,"

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.834
and answer all my questions,
it was just so invaluable.

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.801
So I just make a point
whenever somebody --

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:12.100
When I read
that someone's a superhero,

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.501
I just go like, "If you want
info, like, I'm here.

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:15.901
I'm not, like,
actually Carol Danvers,

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.067
who's always like, super-busy.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:18.601
Like, I'm fine.
Like, you can talk to me."

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:19.634
-"You can talk to me
about everything."

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:21.000
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.367
I'm not always like, "Oh, no,
I'm on a control panel.

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:23.467
I can't talk."
Like, that's her.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:24.934
-Okay, yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:26.801
I have a pretty boring life,
actually, yeah.

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:30.033
-No. I know that you've become
close with one of your co-stars,

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.133
Samuel L. Jackson.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.400
-My bestie.
-Really?

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.434
-Yeah, we're best friends.
Yeah, soul mates, really.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:35.634
-Yeah.
-I know.

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:36.701
It's surprising
to everybody, including us.

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:38.467
-No, but you were
telling me backstage

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.767
that you guys text each other
and stuff like that.

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:42.701
-Oh, well, yes, of course.

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:44.901
I mean, he's really
big on emojis.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:46.434
I can say that.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:49.567
And he's also the person
that will send me, like,

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:51.868
videos of people falling
or, like, videos of, like,

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:54.200
corgis in inner tubes
going down the river, you know?

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.501
And if I don't respond
quick enough,

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.234
he's like, "Are you okay?"

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:59.000
-He's like, "Did you see
my funny video?

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.200
Yeah. Hello?"

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.200
-"Like, the Dr Pepper,
like, went crazy.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.634
Are you not enjoying that?"

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:06.767
So, yes, he's -- We've done,
I think, five movies together,

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:08.033
and we're planning
our next five.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.133
It's just --
Yeah, he's just my favorite.

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:11.434
-Good. I'm so happy.
-Yeah.

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.701
I'm his second favorite, so --
-Oh, is that right?

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:14.934
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:16.701
On "The Marvels," actually,
there was a moment

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:17.701
we were working together,
and they're like,

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:18.734
"Could you do one more take?"

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:19.901
He's like, "Of course,
of course.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:21.701
anything for my
second-favorite co-star."

00:05:21.701 --> 00:05:23.434
And I was like,
"What do you mean?

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:25.033
What are you talking about?
Who's your first?"

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:27.300
And he was like, "Me."

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.200
I mean, I can't fight with that.
-You can't fight with that.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.601
-Yeah, I can't fight with that.
-You got to be second to that.

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:32.801
He's a good guy.

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:34.400
You were saying
in some interview I read

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.167
that you read the script
for "The Marvels" and you go,

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:38.634
"This is unbelievable."

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:40.100
-Oh, yeah, it's bonkers.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.534
-"I don't know how you
can pull this off."

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:43.200
-Yeah. I mean,
it's been, like, a while now

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.400
where I've been like,

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.901
"I can't believe I have
to hold the secret.

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.367
It's just -- It's absurd."

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.334
I mean, there's been things
every day when we were filming,

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:51.434
where I was like,
"If my friends only knew what

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:52.467
I was doing right now --"

00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:53.968
I had to learn
all new skill sets.

00:05:53.968 --> 00:05:57.267
There was a lot that -- Yeah,
we go to planets that are

00:05:57.267 --> 00:05:58.300
pretty cool, yeah.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.434
-Really?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:59.434 --> 00:06:00.801
I think so. I think so.

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:03.734
-I think after the first
you came on the show

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:05.267
and we were talking,
and you were like --

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:07.968
I said, "How much time do you
spend in wires and floating?"

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:10.467
You go, "Ooh, a lot of time."
-Oh, well, yeah.

00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:12.267
-So, you're hung --

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:14.434
I mean, to fly, you have
to be on wires and stuff.

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:15.801
-I mean, If you think about it,
like, if you could fly,

00:06:15.801 --> 00:06:16.834
you probably would.

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:17.934
Like, if I was just, like --

00:06:17.934 --> 00:06:18.968
If you're walking
from here to here,

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:20.033
you're not going to walk over.

00:06:20.033 --> 00:06:21.767
You're going to levitate over.

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:23.467
If you can go 2 inches
off of the ground,

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:24.701
like, you're going to do it.

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.133
Which, like,
seems like a cool idea,

00:06:26.133 --> 00:06:27.367
but just to anybody out there

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:29.033
who's, like, thinking
of becoming a superhero

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.100
or like you're a superhero,
and then, suddenly, you can fly,

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.868
like, just know it means
an eternal wedgie

00:06:32.868 --> 00:06:35.200
for everything you
ever do after that.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.934
Like, you just don't
think about it.

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:38.334
You're like, "Cool!
I can fly. Wow!"

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:39.701
And you do it one time,
you're like, "Peter Pan! Cool!"

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:41.267
And then you're like, "Oh, no!

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:44.133
Actually,
this is so uncomfortable.

00:06:44.133 --> 00:06:45.701
And now I have to be cool
and, like,

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:47.167
talk about, like,
helping people,

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:49.601
but, like, really,,
I'm in a full-body plank,

00:06:49.601 --> 00:06:52.000
and it's just, like --" It's a
lot of core strength, folks.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.567
It's a lot. It's a lot.

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:55.434
And you're just kind of, like,
airlifted up and around

00:06:55.434 --> 00:06:57.501
and you're just, like,
holding that, just being like,

00:06:57.501 --> 00:06:59.367
"We really got to do this. Ugh!"

00:06:59.367 --> 00:07:01.901
It's like -- So, you know,
it's acting is what I'm saying.

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:03.334
-Yeah, it's acting.
-It's acting.

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:05.868
-But I have a couple
behind-the-scenes clips

00:07:05.868 --> 00:07:07.501
that you brought just
for us of you in rehearsal.

00:07:07.501 --> 00:07:08.901
-Oh, I hope they're cool.
-Yeah.

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:10.601
Well, let's check
this first one out here.

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:12.534
Let's just...

00:07:12.534 --> 00:07:14.801
Look at the --
You see the wires here.

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:16.701
There's the wires.
You walk out to the front yard.

00:07:16.701 --> 00:07:19.934
"Hey, what's up guys?
How you doing?"

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:22.300
And whoa!

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.167
I mean, that's fun.
-That is fun.

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:26.968
That is fun.
-But that's amazing.

00:07:26.968 --> 00:07:28.200
-Yeah.
-But then --

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:29.834
-That's my job, guys.
Like, that's my job.

00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:31.400
-Yeah, that's your job.
-So that's wild.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:32.868
-I want to show another one.

00:07:32.868 --> 00:07:34.901
Here's a clip of you on these
wires of acting and fighting.

00:07:34.901 --> 00:07:35.934
-Action!
-Okay.

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:38.734
-Look at this.
-Fly! Punch, punch!

00:07:38.734 --> 00:07:41.634
Fly! Land, punch.

00:07:41.634 --> 00:07:43.767
-I mean, come on!
That is a pro.

00:07:43.767 --> 00:07:45.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.200
-That's a pro right there.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.367
-Just like
a little burger order.

00:07:47.367 --> 00:07:48.567
"Fly, punch, punch,
land, punch."

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:50.701
-"Fly, land, punch."
-Yeah, of course.

00:07:50.701 --> 00:07:52.834
-What do we say about
"The Marvels"?, except for --

00:07:52.834 --> 00:07:54.067
-What do we say?
-Yeah.

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:55.200
Well, I know
we're not really allowed to say.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.501
-I don't think we're allowed
to say anything.

00:07:56.501 --> 00:07:58.567
